// An undefined variable renders identically under both engines: the same
// suggestion (searched over the same names, in the same order, defined-only),
// the same situational help line, and the same caret position — pinned to the
// innermost enclosing call, exactly where the interpreter's Node.locate puts it.
val nearby = 42

// The suggestion comes from the program's own globals once they hold a value...
println(attempt(() -> nearbyy).error.help)
// ...never from the misspelled name itself, and a hopeless typo gets no
// suggestion at all, only the assignment note.
println(attempt(() -> zzqqxjw).error.help)
// A '_' name explains privacy instead of assignment order.
println(attempt(() -> _hidden).error.help)
// A builtin can be the nearest match too.
println(attempt(() -> lenn([1])).error.help)

// Inside a function body the error reports the call that entered it, and the
// traceback names that call site — one frame, even through the tail call the
// arrow lambda makes.
def f() {
    totallyUndefined
}
val r = attempt(() -> f())
println(r.error.message, r.error.trace)

// Uncaught, on the last line, inside a nested call: stderr must carry the same
// message, the same "--> file:line:col", the same caret column, both help
// lines, and exit status 1 under both engines.
println(max(1, x))
